ed States  legally either as tourists or  overstaying other types of visas if you  really want to deal with the number of  people that are in the United States  illegally undocumented beyond the amount  of time that they were supposed to be  here then you would realize that the  number of physical border crossings is  actually not the majority of the people  that are here and you  deploy resources elsewhere would it be  cheap absolutely not would it be  efficient I don't know those people are  spread out across the United States but  if you are serious about fixing the  problem you identify that would be a  place to focus more energy very  importantly sue and find companies that  hire undocumented immigrants this  includes Donald Trump's companies Donald  Trump's personal housekeeper we found  out at his New Jersey Golf Club was an  undocumented immigrant  in the United States if they cannot get  jobs in the United States remember  they're coming here to work they're not  lazy many are going to stop coming here  and as I've said before companies love  this companies want to have people here  that they can hire particularly people  who will number one accept low salaries  because there are they going to complain  their status here is in question and who  are vulnerable knowing that they are  here illegally so they are unlikely to  complain about working conditions or  anything else so we need to actually  start punishing the companies we have a  legal infrastructure to do that members  of Congress benefit from undocumented  immigration the social welfare system  benefits from undocumented immigration  because contrary to what you often hear  you have people paying into the system  who are here illegally who are never  going to get benefits out because they  are here illegally it's free money for  the welfare social welfare system and  many programs not all obviously if  you're not paying into that you're  you're not part of what I'm saying but  many undocumented immi